WEBVTT

00:38:28.719 --> 00:38:32.326
this has happened to me probably six times
in the last four or five years --

00:38:32.350 --> 00:38:34.999
I say to myself, "You know,
I'm going to write a column

00:38:35.023 --> 00:38:37.347
where I admit that immigration
is really complex,

00:38:37.371 --> 00:38:39.507
and that it's economically
a very mixed bag.

00:38:39.531 --> 00:38:41.799
It hurts people from low-wage jobs."

00:38:41.823 --> 00:38:44.997
And then I look at the data,
and I just don't find it there.

00:38:45.021 --> 00:38:48.041
I find that immigration boosts growth.

00:38:48.065 --> 00:38:51.417
It doesn't actually that much cut into
the wages of low-wage jobs,

00:38:51.441 --> 00:38:54.955
because it pushes other people,
the earlier inhabitants up the wage scale,

00:38:54.979 --> 00:38:56.137
up the job scale.

00:38:56.161 --> 00:38:59.020
So I just don't find evidence to argue

00:38:59.044 --> 00:39:03.695
that it's this thing that is really
sucking down the lower middle class.